| variant | opp | W/D/L | points | mean margin | world 95% CI (mine) |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| terminal | m26 | 24/0/8 | 24/32 (.75) | +$190.22 | [+96.2, +298.6] |
| terminal | tetsu | 16/0/0 | 16/16 | +$23,138 | — |
| terminal | ozer44 | 14/0/2 | 14/16 | +$19,987 | — |
| a1 | m26 | 8/16/8 | 16/32 | $0.00 | [0, 0] |
| a1 | tetsu | 16/0/0 | 16/16 | +$23,269 | — |
| a1 | ozer44 | 14/0/2 | 14/16 | +$19,954 | — |
| dsm75_mg25 | m26 | 15/0/17 | 15/32 | −$1,922.56 | [−3,951, +74] |
| dsm75_mg25 | tetsu | 16/0/0 | 16/16 | +$13,297 | — |
| dsm75_mg25 | ozer44 | 16/0/0 | 16/16 | +$16,945 | — |

Matches Codex's terminal figures (+190.21875, CI [96.81, 299.44]; bootstrap RNG differs only).
Gate as frozen: **terminal PASS; a1 FAIL; dsm75_mg25 FAIL.**

## Interpretation
- **terminal.** Against m26, the a1 games are a pure m26 mirror (16/16 worlds exactly antisymmetric), so a paired own-cash
  delta can be computed per game: **32/32 ≥ 0 (min $0, mean +$190.2); opponent reward changes by exactly $0 in all 32**. So the
  effect is a pure end-of-game own-cash gain, not harm to the opponent. The 24/32 points come from turning mirror draws into
  +$23…+$134 wins; that is not evidence of a rating gain against the field. The real effect is ≈ +$190/game (~0.2% of a
  typical $70–115k score): it can only decide very close games. It is low-risk and monotone.
- **Sanity confound (not a terminal defect).** In the tetsu/ozer44 sanity games, 28/32 terminal-vs-a1 pairs differ only in own cash
  (+$0…+$1,081, opp Δ 0). Two worlds (both seats) diverge **before** step 718 (opponent reward also changes): ozer44 93047105
  (terminal −$6,413 vs a1) and tetsu 93047103 (−$1,812). Terminal equals m26 before 718, so the most likely explanation is that
  **A1 did activate there** and helped (+$6.4k / +$1.8k); nondeterminism in tetsu/ozer44 is the other explanation. Resolving it
  needs 2 games (m26 vs ozer44 w93047105 and m26 vs tetsu w93047103, seat 0); I didn't run them because I was told not to
  launch games. Either way the terminal-only delta in the 28 clean pairs is ≥ 0.
- **a1.** Inactive in the whole h2h panel, so the h2h gate cannot measure it (it did not "fail" on effect). It may be active against
  stronger/herding opponents (see above). No promotion from this evidence.
- **dsm75_mg25.** Clear regression: −$1,923/game vs m26 (CI upper barely +$74) and much lower sanity margins than a1/terminal
  (tetsu +$13.3k vs +$23.3k; ozer44 +$16.9k vs +$20.0k). Reject.

## Recommendation
terminal may be frozen via `package.py` **after** the refreshed `summary.json` and the 6/6 loader-smoke parity. The README must
describe the gain as ≈ +$190/game own cash, never negative in paired play; the 75% h2h points should not be presented as a
strength signal. The human decides on submission; no agent submits.
- [ ] 2026-09-30T09:03Z from claude: T047 code review (Claude): PASS, no blocking defects -> research/t047_code_review_claude.md. Key: terminal own-cash delta vs pure mirror is >=0 in 32/32 h2h games, opp reward unchanged, mean +$190.2 (=world CI since mirror world mean is exactly 0); A1 never activated (16/16 worlds exact antisymmetric margins = pure mirror); points>=.65 is mostly tie-breaking of exact mirror draws. Suggest logging _HG_STATS overrides per game. Result review follows if 192 finish shortly.
- [ ] 2026-09-30T09:05Z from claude: T047 RESULT review (Claude) -> research/t047_result_review_claude.md. All 192 done, 0 invalid/errors, overage untouched. Recomputed: terminal PASS (24/32, +$190.22, CI[96.2,298.6]); a1 FAIL (inactive in all 16 h2h worlds); dsm75_mg25 FAIL (-$1922.6, CI[-3951,+74], weaker sanity). Terminal paired own delta vs pure mirror >=0 in 32/32, opp delta 0. NOTE summary.json on disk is STALE (187 rec, complete=false): rerun summarize.py + loader_smoke.py before package.py. Sanity confound: ozer44 w93047105 & tetsu w93047103 terminal vs a1 diverge pre-718 (opp reward changes) -> A1 likely active there (+$6.4k/+$1.8k); 2 m26 games would resolve it.

